Port radxa's debian/patches/fix-linux-7.1-build.patch to the SDIO tree.

Upstream wrote that patch against the USB tree only (src/USB/...), so the SDIO
driver we build still had the pre-7.1 prototypes and did not compile on 7.1.
Linux 7.1 changed the cfg80211_ops key and station callbacks, plus
cfg80211_new_sta()/cfg80211_del_sta(), to take a struct wireless_dev * in place
of a struct net_device *, and flattened the TDLS discovery-response action
frame (u.action.u.tdls_discover_resp -> u.action.tdls_discover_resp, with
action_code in the generic action header).

Every change is gated on LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7, 1, 0), so the
pre-7.1 build path is unchanged. The hunks mirror the upstream USB patch
one-for-one; only the surrounding source (indentation and layout) differs.

